TASK
1. STRUCTURE — the blueprint must contain, as ## headings: The decision; Executive summary; The engagement — context and scope; Where you are today; The opportunity; How this makes money; The product, module by module; What we'd build first; What success looks like. Flag any missing or empty. The decision must make ONE forceful choice (a "First:" and a "Not yet:" verdict) — a decision section that merely lists options is an empty decision and a high finding.
2. CONSISTENCY — the document must not contradict the layers: every module named in the document exists in the module list and vice versa; the scope obeys the register (a capability engagement never redesigns the whole business — and recommendations stay inside the stated geography); the executive summary's claims appear in the body. The document must never state the same fact two different ways (a settlement cycle given as both "2 days" and "monthly", two different volumes for the same operation), and a figure must keep ONE frequency everywhere — a weekly number reused as monthly is a high finding. The decision's Phase 1 pilot must never be described as predictive AI, risk scoring, or an "engine" — a Phase 1 wearing an AI name is a high finding.
3. COVERAGE — the structured layers live ALONGSIDE the document (they render as their own sections and pages); their absence from the document text is CORRECT and never a finding. A coverage finding exists only when a layer's COUNT above is zero: no journey stages, no scoreboard rows, no risks, or no quick wins.

Respond with ONLY this JSON shape, no markdown fences, no commentary:

{
  "checks": [
    {"label": "All canonical sections present", "passed": true|false, "note": "<one sentence>"},
    {"label": "Documents consistent with the structured layers", "passed": true|false, "note": "<one sentence>"},
    {"label": "Scope obeys the engagement register", "passed": true|false, "note": "<one sentence>"}
  ],
  "findings": [
    {"severity": "high|low", "where": "<section>", "issue": "<what is missing or contradictory>", "fix": "<what to add or correct>"}
  ]
}

findings must be empty when everything passes. Never invent problems to look diligent.
